SAFETY AND QUALITY REVIEW / KNOWN LIMITATIONS
All ten complete SKILL.md bodies, both complete LICENSE texts and the included
story-bank reference were read during selection, not merely their metadata.
No selected file directs credential collection, secret extraction/upload,
destructive system changes, executable installation, automatic application
submission or automatic sending of candidate documents/messages. Examples are
illustrations, NEVER facts about the user. Unsupported numbers, certifications,
skills, achievements or competing offers must not be invented. Missing evidence
must be asked for, omitted or visibly marked, not filled with examples.

The five open-career-skills files retain upstream promotional closing sentences
linking to JobMentis. These are third-party advertising, NOT a MINOS endorsement,
requirement or integration. Users do NOT need to visit, register, purchase or
upload anything there to use these Markdown skills. The included files do not
implement a network upload. Do not send personal data to these links.

ats-detective can make unauthenticated requests to PUBLIC employer job boards;
company names/board slugs go into URLs, not resumes. Ask before network use and
do not transmit private candidate data. URL matches and board probes identify
only observed evidence, not guaranteed employer-wide systems. Upstream claims
about each ATS vendor's parsing/ranking behavior are generalized, unverified
heuristics; they are NOT guarantees, screening probabilities or benchmark data.
Likewise resume keyword scores are heuristics, not actual employer ATS results.

salary-negotiation-prep contains unsourced statistics (including '84%') and
US-centric salary-history, benefits and tax assumptions. Do not present those
statistics as verified facts; validate current sources and local law. Equity
and compensation examples simplify liquidity, vesting, taxation and risk;
recalculate arithmetic against actual offers and consult qualified local
legal/tax/financial advice where appropriate. No hiring, pay or ATS result is
promised. Formatting preferences are market-specific, not universal rules.

WORKSPACE CONVENTIONS / OPTIONAL CROSS-SKILL REFERENCES
The open-career skills refer to user-owned profile/profile.md, story-bank/,
tracker/applications.md and output/ paths. These are workspace conventions, NOT
files containing a bundled user's profile. Ask the user for inputs if absent;
do not search outside the authorized workspace. The original STAR format guide
is available in the installed star-story-extractor/story-bank/README.md; consult
that guide when creating the user's workspace story-bank. Never overwrite an
existing user file merely to satisfy a convention. Slash commands in upstream
text are upstream shortcuts, not additional MINOS commands or integrations.
resume-tailor mentions job-description-analyzer; that optional upstream skill
is NOT bundled. Analyze the user's supplied JD directly instead. All required
instructional content for the selected ten skills is included, with no external
executable dependency or credential required.

REJECTED CANDIDATES (NOT BUNDLED)
From Paramchoudhary/ResumeSkills: resume-bullet-writer, resume-ats-optimizer,
interview-prep-generator, job-description-analyzer, career-changer-translator:
examples or quantification instructions add facts not grounded in the supplied
input, risking fabricated candidate achievements/skills; no silent repair made.
linkedin-profile-optimizer was not selected: weak fact constraints and dated
platform claims. cover-letter-generator was superseded by the stricter factual
cover-letter-writer rather than duplicating that role.
From squerne/open-career-skills: job-search explicitly acknowledges its proposed
LinkedIn automated fetching is against that site's terms; not bundled.
linkedin-360brew-planner demands treating unverified ranking rules as established
facts; not bundled. evidence-miner was not selected because it depends on git
operations instead of being purely document-first.

